-- FINDING 1 (loud).  `@effective` and `@repealed`, the decorators for same-named versioned rules, are not in this
-- build.  The tutorial and TEMPORAL-RULE-VERSION-DESIGN.md (Phase 2) describe them as planned.
--
-- Expected on a build that has them: one dispatcher over two same-named rules.
-- Printed by the unstable build (the shelf build and the early dev build alike): two warnings "Unknown annotation `@effective` ... ignored", then an ERROR,
-- "There are multiple definitions for the identifier `rate`", because the two same-named rules are both live.
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

TIMEZONE IS "Asia/Singapore"

@effective 2003-07-31
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rate` MEANS 7

@effective 2011-01-01
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rate` MEANS 9

#EVAL `rate`
